Can you point out a specific case where a monster with no hands will be
doing something that typically would require a monster to have hands?

I understand the point you're trying to make, but I also note that by
and large this is actually covered in gameplay; I don't recall any
jarring instances of "it wields a weapon in what hand?!" or anything
like that, so ... is this really a current problem?

> What if later on I try to make a patch which means that the player can 
> only cast "finger of death" when he is in a form which has hands?

Well, I'd _expect_ you to go through the monster flags and monsters to
get a quick idea of what exactly was out there.  ;)  But OK, you might
miss an interaction.

> I can't use NOHANDS to achieve this goal, because a gelatinous cube player 
> could still cast FoD.

Yup.  And if the player selfpolying into cubeland and casting FoD
worried you enough, you could add a check and say "also, NOLIMBS".  

Or you could create a NOCAST flag, for monsters who simply aren't to be
allowed to cast spells due to lack of whatever spell-casting mechanism
you're thinking of.

Or you could consider that a gelatinous cube might easily be able to form
part of itself into a hand-like appendage, and thus create a 'hand' that
way.  

(Yeah, I know, that's a semi-rationalization, but this is not something
entirely new to Nethack.  :)

> Of course, there could be some clever reason the NetHack source is 
> structured this way, but it just seems kinda arbitrary to me.

You'd have to ask the person who originally added the NOHANDS flag.

